I've made the following changes:
1. Added the `userCredentialIds` array to the app object in the preview component
2. Added `credentialId` to the credentialOwner object to match the expected structure

This should resolve the TypeError that was occurring when trying to call `.some()` on undefined. The `useIsAppEnabled` hook now has all the required properties it needs to function correctly.

The error was occurring because the hook expects either `userCredentialIds` or `credentialOwner.credentialId` to be present in the app object to properly determine if the app is enabled for a specific credential. By providing these properties in the preview data, we ensure that the hook can properly check the credential status.

